WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:01.620
- [Instructor] Let's
see if we can figure out

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:06.620
what two divided by 0.1 or one tenth is.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.070
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.730
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.010
And there's a couple of ways
that we can approach it.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.420
One way is to think about
everything in terms of tenths.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.060
So two wholes is how many tenths?

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.280
Well, a whole is equal to 10 tenths,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.520
so two wholes is equal to 20 tenths.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.403
So I could write the two,
rewrite the two, as 20 tenths.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.543
And so that's going to
be 20 tenths divided by,

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.330
and instead of writing
it this way, I could,

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.160
instead of just writing it as 0.1,

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.170
we know this is the
same thing as one tenth.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.623
So divided by one tenth.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.400
And so if I have 20 of something

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.310
and if I divide it by, into
groups of one of that something,

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.170
how many groups am I going to have?

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:59.610
Well, I'm going to have
20 equal groups of one.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:03.830
So 20 tenths divided by
one tenth is equal to 20.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.060
Another way that you
could approach that is

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.360
you could rewrite the 0.1,
the one tenth, as a fraction.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:15.360
We could rewrite this as
two divided by, divided by,

00:01:16.629 --> 00:01:18.028
instead of writing one tenth like this,

00:01:18.028 --> 00:01:21.430
I could write it as a
fraction, divided by 1/10.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:24.560
Well, we know that dividing by a tenth is

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.300
the same thing as multiplying by 10.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:33.300
So this is going to be equal
to two times, two times 10.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.470
And that gets us to the same
place that we had before.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:40.840
What is two times 10?

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.840
Well, that is going to be equal to 20.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.160
That's good, that we
got to the same answer,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.460
otherwise these would not
be equivalent methods.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.310
Let's do another example.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.020
So let's say we wanted to figure out

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:59.020
what six divided by one tenth is.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.150
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.370
All right, well, you
could do the same idea.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.500
Six wholes is equal to how many tenths?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.680
It's equal to 60 tenths.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:15.680
So I'll rewrite this as 60
tenths, divided by one tenth,

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:23.530
is equal to how many, is equal to what?

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.500
Well, if I have 60 of
something and if I divide it

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.170
into groups of one of that something,

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.550
I'm gonna have 60 equal groups of one.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.510
So this is going to be equal to 60.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.840
So you might see a pattern.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.720
When we divide it by a tenth,
we end up multiplying by 10.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.320
When we divide by a tenth,
we are multiplying by 10.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.530
And you could do the same
thing as we saw up here.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.880
You could take, you could
say six divided by one tenth

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.880
is the same thing as
six divided by one tenth

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:56.080
written as a fraction, which
is going to be equal to

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.820
six times, you could say six times 10

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.370
or six times 10 over one, either way.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:05.750
Six times 10 over one.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.240
Or, which is the same thing as 10,

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.100
which is once again
going to be equal to 60.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.410
So I think you see the general pattern.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:15.060
Divide by a tenth, same
thing as multiplying by 10.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.920
Now, what about if we
dealt with hundredths?

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.610
So let's say we wanna figure out

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:24.610
what seven divided by a hundredth is.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.233
What would this be?

00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:29.040
Pause the video and try to figure it out.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.520
All right, well, we can do the same drill.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.050
So seven wholes, one whole is
equal to a hundred hundredths,

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:39.520
so seven wholes is
equal to 700 hundredths.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.398
So this is equal to,
I'll write it like this,

00:03:42.398 --> 00:03:47.398
700 hundredths, hundredths, divided by,

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:54.220
divided by one hundredth, one hundredth.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:57.240
If I have 700 of something
and if I'm dividing it

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.290
into equal groups of
one of that something,

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.760
I'm gonna have 700 equal groups.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.800
So this is going to be equal to 700.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.200
So you divide by a hundredth,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.430
is the same thing as
multiplying by a hundred.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:12.480
Now, you could also rewrite
this as fraction if you like,

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.540
so that some of the principles
we saw up here still apply.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:20.540
So we could rewrite this
as seven divided by 1/100,

00:04:21.821 --> 00:04:24.220
and so this is going
to be the same thing as

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:28.430
seven times a hundred over
one, or seven times a hundred.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:33.430
Seven times 100, which, once
again, will get you to 700.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.540
So I think you see a pattern.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:39.920
Divide by a tenth, same
thing as multiplying by 10.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.150
Divide by a hundredth, same thing as

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.403
multiplying by a hundred.

